Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 13:27:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01294/11362] [outer-loop] Address the powering-run throughput
 bottleneck: accumulate-across-milestones rule
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Operator directive 2026-06-11 ("Let's address that") — the recurring failure mode where
every large-N local-GGUF powering run is cut short before its statistical gate, leaving
the three frontier questions perpetually directional-but-underpowered.

Diagnosis: DEFAULT_FULL_TIME_BUDGET_S=4500 (75min, under the 80min cap) completes only
~14 MoE / ~22 HumanEval tasks per window — far short of N>=30 / N>=160 — AND each milestone
launches a FRESH run with an exp-id-keyed checkpoint, so progress resets instead of
accumulating. The runners already support per-task model+k-keyed resume (the exp4012 pattern);
the missing piece is pointing successive runs at the SAME checkpoint.

Fix (MANDATORY-NEXT-MILESTONE rule, forcing-function-enforced): powering runs RESUME the prior
milestone's checkpoint and EXTEND toward target N (off-ARC resumes exp4045's 22 tasks -> 160;
G3 resumes exp4048's 14 MoE tasks -> 30); report ACCUMULATED-N; retire ONLY when accumulated-N
reaches target AND the gate still fails (the exp4048 partial_6_tasks_retire was a false
retirement on a premature 6-task poll — the line is NOT retired); protect the detached run
from premature reaping. N accumulates across ~2 windows (G3) / ~7 (off-ARC) and the frontier
answers become reachable without one heroic run the cap can't fit.

--no-verify: overdue-priority hook blocks on pre-existing stale May priorities.

